WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
Existing weight-modification methods like OWM treat
every input the same when constraining updates.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.200
But in fake audio detection,

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.840
genuine speech tends to look similar from one
dataset to the next,

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.480
while the fake speech varies.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.120
That regularity is an opportunity: the direction of
a weight update should adapt to how

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.760
much of a batch is genuine versus fake.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.400
At the same time,

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.040
some datasets collect genuine audio under acoustic
conditions so different that a naive rule backfires,

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.680
motivating an extra safeguard.
